title "O365 Platform (Fly)"
layout row
subtitle "SaaS with On Prem/Cloud Exchange Servers and Active Directory"

# not modelled: legend, domain colour key, "Updated" date, footnote
# ("*All platform apps would have a dependency to the platform host prod environment")

BC manage-tech: Manage Technology
BC offer-tech: Offer Technology

BA o365: O365 E5
BA teams: Teams
BA sharepoint: SharePoint Online
BA exchange: Exchange
BA ad: Active Directory

SI o365-prod: O365 Prod
SI teams-saas: Teams SaaS
SI sharepoint-saas: SharePoint SaaS
SI exchange-prod: Exchange On Prem Prod [Dev]
SI ad-prod: Active Directory 2022 Prod

BSO teams-bso: Teams
BSO sharepoint-sites: SharePoint Sites
BSO outlook: Outlook
BS messaging: Direct Messaging Services
BS file-sharing: File Sharing Services
BS email: Email Services

TMSO aad-admin: Azure Active Directory Administration
TMSO exchange-admin: Exchange Administration
TMSO windows-admin: Windows Server Admin
TMS identity: Identity Access Services
TMS app-mgmt: Application Mgmt Services
TMS compute: Compute Services

DCG windows-group: Windows Exchange Servers
CI(Application) exchange-app: Exchange
CI(Windows Server) windows: Exchange01, Exchange02

SP tech-portfolio: Technology Portfolio
SP comm-portfolio: Communication

manage-tech -> o365
# strategic: purple connector Manage Technology <-> Identity Access, continued by a
# second purple line down the TMS column to Compute Services; all three TMS
manage-tech -> identity
manage-tech -> app-mgmt
manage-tech -> compute
# strategic: one purple connector from Offer Technology runs down the BS column
# behind Direct Messaging and File Sharing (glued to Email Services); all three
offer-tech -> messaging
offer-tech -> file-sharing
offer-tech -> email

# platform host
teams -> o365
sharepoint -> o365
exchange -> o365
teams -> teams-saas
sharepoint -> sharepoint-saas
exchange -> exchange-prod
ad -> ad-prod

teams-saas -> o365-prod
sharepoint-saas -> o365-prod
exchange-prod -> o365-prod
# "Sends Data to" is one dash-dot connector glued to Teams SaaS that runs up the
# instance column behind Exchange and SharePoint SaaS; read as all three
ad-prod -> teams-saas : Sends Data to
ad-prod -> sharepoint-saas : Sends Data to
ad-prod -> exchange-prod : Sends Data to

teams-bso -> teams-saas
sharepoint-sites -> sharepoint-saas
outlook -> exchange-prod
teams-bso -> messaging
sharepoint-sites -> file-sharing
outlook -> email
# one dashed connector Direct Messaging -> Communication runs behind the BS column
messaging -> comm-portfolio
file-sharing -> comm-portfolio
email -> comm-portfolio

aad-admin -> ad-prod
aad-admin -> identity
exchange-admin -> exchange-app
exchange-admin -> app-mgmt
windows-admin -> windows-group
windows-admin -> compute
windows-group -> windows
# the blue service-mapping connector starts at the Dev back card (drawn to the stack here) and runs behind
# Application Exchange to the Windows servers stack; read as the stack -> app -> servers
exchange-prod -> exchange-app
exchange-app -> windows

identity -> tech-portfolio
app-mgmt -> tech-portfolio
compute -> tech-portfolio
